 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "The principal of an elementary school plans to visit each classroom exactly once before leaving for the day. The floor plan of the school is given. Use this information for the following exercises.\n<br>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/500fd3a13e8aab63.png\" alt=\"A floor plan of an elementary school. It has three blocks. The first block has front office A. The second block has three rooms: G, H, and I. The third block has five rooms: B, C, D, E, and F. Exit is at the top-right.\">\n",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 329770,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Draw a graph to represent the floor plan for the elementary school in which each vertex is a room and an edge between two vertices indicates that there is a path between the two rooms that does not pass the door to another room.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 329771,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Use your graph to find a route that the principal can take beginning at the Front Office in room <i>A</i>, visiting each room exactly once (without passing by another room), and ending at room <i>F</i>, which is next to the exit.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 329772,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Would the route you found be best to trace out a Hamilton path, an Euler trail, both, or neither in the graph you drew? Explain how you know. \n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  }
 ],
